THIRD-PARTY WORK REFERENCED

Personality framework
    The sixteen-type matching heuristic in ollie/types16.py is our own weighting, derived
    from arguments in "Gifts Differing: Understanding Personality Type" by Isabel Briggs
    Myers with Peter B. Myers. The book is not included or redistributed. The weights and
    all descriptive text in that module are written by us.

Personality items
    The onboarding questionnaire uses items in the style of the International Personality
    Item Pool (https://ipip.ori.org), whose materials are in the public domain.

Humanizer, https://github.com/blader/humanizer (MIT)
    An agent skill, not a runtime dependency. Its catalogue of AI writing patterns
    informed the rule set in ollie/style.py, which is our own implementation in code.

Graphify, https://github.com/safishamsi/graphify (pip: graphifyy)
    An optional extra, used only over sanitised episode cards. Not bundled, not required,
    and not on any code path the product depends on.

Ollama, https://ollama.com
    Spoken to over its local HTTP API. Not bundled. Each model carries its own licence,
    which the user accepts when they download it.

